afeguards/s3/p49","ftc-safeguards/s3/p50","ftc-safeguards/s3/p51","ftc-safeguards/s3/p52","ftc-safeguards/s3/p53","ftc-safeguards/s3/p54","ftc-safeguards/s3/p55","ftc-safeguards/s3/p56","hipaa-breach/s4/p0","hipaa-breach/s4/p1","hipaa-breach/s4/p2"]},{"key":"the_firm","label":"the_firm","value":6,"n":6,"ids":["hipaa-security/s6/p12","hipaa-breach/s5/p0","hipaa-breach/s5/p1","hipaa-breach/s5/p2","hipaa-breach/s5/p3","hipaa-breach/s5/p4"]},{"key":"unspecified","label":"unspecified","value":4,"n":4,"ids":["hipaa-breach/s6/p0","hipaa-breach/s6/p1","hipaa-breach/s6/p2","hipaa-breach/s7/p1"]},{"key":"media_public","label":"media_public","value":3,"n":3,"ids":["hipaa-breach/s3/p0","hipaa-breach/s3/p1","hipaa-breach/s3/p2"]}],"total":489},{"id":"v_rows","type":"table","title":"Reg S-P duties for a broker-dealer, most time-pressured first","why":"The rows to read.","x":"obligation_type","y":"timeframe","measure":"count","measure_field":"timeframe","cols":["obligation_type","timeframe","timeframe"],"rows":[{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p4","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶5","text":"(iii) Protect against unauthorized access to or use of customer information that could result in substantial harm or inconvenience to any customer.","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p3","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶4","text":"(ii) Protect against any anticipated threats or hazards to the security or integrity of customer information; and","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p8","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶9","text":"(iii) Notify each affected individual whose sensitive customer information was, or is reasonably likely to have been, accessed or used without authorization in accordance with paragraph (a)(4) of this section unless the covered institution determines, after a  …","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p7","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶8","text":"(ii) Take appropriate steps to contain and control the incident to prevent further unauthorized access to or use of customer information; and","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p5","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶6","text":"(3) Response programs for unauthorized access to or use of customer information. Written policies and procedures in paragraph (a)(1) of this section must include a program reasonably designed to detect, respond to, and recover from unauthorized access to or us …","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p9","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶10","text":"(4) Notifying affected individuals of unauthorized access or use—(i) Notification obligation. Unless a covered institution has determined, after a reasonable investigation of the facts and circumstances of the incident of unauthorized access to or use of sensi …","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p6","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶7","text":"(i) Assess the nature and scope of any incident involving unauthorized access to or use of customer information and identify the customer information systems and types of customer information that may have been accessed or used without authorization;","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p10","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶11","text":"(ii) Affected individuals. If an incident of unauthorized access to or use of customer information has occurred or is reasonably likely to have occurred, but the covered institution is unable to identify which specific individuals' sensitive customer informati …","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p11","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶12","text":"(iii) Timing. A covered institution must provide the notice as soon as practicable, but not later than 30 days, after becoming aware that unauthorized access to or use of customer information has occurred or is reasonably likely to have occurred unless the Uni …","cells":["notification","Within 30 days or less","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p13","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶14","text":"(A) Describe in general terms the incident and the type of sensitive customer information that was or is reasonably believed to have been accessed or used without authorization;","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p23","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶24","text":"(B) Provide notification to the covered institution as soon as possible, but no later than 72 hours after becoming aware that a breach in security has occurred resulting in unauthorized access to a customer information system maintained by the service provider …","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p20","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶21","text":"(H) Include information about the availability of online guidance from the Federal Trade Commission and usa.gov regarding steps an individual can take to protect against identity theft, a statement encouraging the individual to report any incidents of identity …","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p17","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶18","text":"(E) Explain what a fraud alert is and how an individual may place a fraud alert in the individual's credit reports to put the individual's creditors on notice that the individual may be a victim of fraud, including identity theft;","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p21","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶22","text":"(5) Service providers. (i) A covered institution's response program prepared in accordance with paragraph (a)(3) of this section must include the establishment, maintenance, and enforcement of written policies and procedures reasonably designed to require over …","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p22","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶23","text":"(A) Protect against unauthorized access to or use of customer information; and","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p2","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶3","text":"(i) Ensure the security and confidentiality of customer information;","cells":["incident_response","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p14","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶15","text":"(B) Include, if the information is reasonably possible to determine at the time the notice is provided, any of the following: the date of the incident, the estimated date of the incident, or the date range within which the incident occurred;","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p12","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶13","text":"(iv) Notice contents. The notice must:","cells":["notification","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p25","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶26","text":"(iii) Notwithstanding a covered institution's use of a service provider in accordance with paragraphs (a)(5)(i) and (ii) of this section, the obligation to ensure that affected individuals are notified in accordance with paragraph (a)(4) of this section rests  …","cells":["notification","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p16","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶17","text":"(D) If the individual has an account with the covered institution, recommend that the customer review account statements and immediately report any suspicious activity to the covered institution;","cells":["vendor_oversight","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]}],"total":40}],"insights":{"answer":"Add an Anthropic API key to get a written analysis. These observations are computed directly from the views.","insights":[{"title":"Reg S-P obligations that bind broker-dealers","body":"40 (40 of 489 rows).","view_ids":["v_bd"],"unit_ids":["reg-sp/s0/p0","reg-sp/s0/p1","reg-sp/s0/p2","reg-sp/s0/p3","reg-sp/s0/p4"]},{"title":"Obligation mix by regulation","body":"Densest cell: safeguards × hipaa-security (78 rows).","view_ids":["v_mix"],"unit_ids":["hipaa-security/s2/p0","hipaa-security/s2/p1","hipaa-security/s2/p2","hipaa-security/s2/p14","hipaa-security/s2/p19"]},{"title":"Which Reg S-P duties are already covered elsewhere","body":"15 relationships found: 15 partial_overlap.","view_ids":["v_overlap"],"unit_ids":[]},{"title":"How fast each rule demands action","body":"Densest cell: No time requirement stated × hipaa-security (108 rows).","view_ids":["v_speed"],"unit_ids":["hipaa-security/s0/p0","hipaa-security/s2/p1","hipaa-security/s2/p2","hipaa-security/s2/p3","hipaa-security/s2/p4"]},{"title":"Who gets notified","body":"Largest: individuals (32), regulator (12), the_firm (6).","view_ids":["v_whom"],"unit_ids":["hipaa-breach/s2/p0","hipaa-breach/s2/p2","hipaa-breach/s2/p3","hipaa-breach/s2/p4","hipaa-breach/s2/p5"]}],"caveats":[],"next_questions":[],"fallback":true}}